.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii $FILENAME
.\"
.\"
.TH TPM2KEY-TOOL "8" "@DATE@" "@PCR_ORACLE_VERSION@" "Parse and Compare TPM 2.0 Keys"
.SH NAME
tpm2key-tool \- parse and compare TPM 2.0 key files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpm2key-tool
.RB [ \-d | \-\-debug ]
.B parse
.I key-file
.P
.B tpm2key-tool
.RB [ \-d | \-\-debug ]
.B cmp
.I key-file-1
.I key-file-2
.P
.B tpm2key-tool
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tpm2key-tool
is a command-line utility designed to parse, inspect, and compare
TPM 2.0 private key files. These files are typically stored in the standard
ASN.1 DER-encoded format defined by the TPM2.0 key file specification (TSS
PrivKey).
.SH OPTIONS
The following options are recognized by
.B tpm2key-tool\fR:
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI parse " key-file"
Decodes and prints a detailed, human-readable summary of the specified
TPM 2.0 key file. This includes structural elements such as:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
The TSSPrivKey type (OID)
.IP \(bu 2
The key's description (if present)
.IP \(bu 2
The parent handle and public key
.IP \(bu 2
Any option or authorization policies (including policy steps and command codes)
.RE
.TP
.BI cmp " key-file-1 key-file-2"
Compares two TPM 2.0 key files to determine if they share the same base key. This
is particularly useful for verifying if two keys were derived or wrapped under
the same parent or if they represent the same underlying TPM object with different
policies.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The utility returns the following exit status codes:
.TP
.B 0
Success, and for the
.B cmp
subcommand, both key files represent or share the same base key.
.TP
.B 1
Returned by the
.B cmp
subcommand only: the keys are valid but do not share the same base key.
.TP
.B 2
An error occurred, such as invalid usage, or a specified key file could not be
read, parsed, or decoded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcr-oracle (8)
